/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A temperature rise T (K) gives a free strain α T, where α is the coefficient of thermal expansion (about 23 × 10⁻⁶ per K for aluminium, 12 × 10⁻⁶ per K for steel).
   - RT is the free thermal radius of curvature (m); h is the depth (m); Ttop and Tbot are the face temperatures (K or °C, only the difference matters).
   - In general the actual strain ε is plane, ε = ε₀ + y/R (plus an x term), and the stress is σ = E(ε − α T).
   - For a boom section the free case has a neat recipe.
   - Ti is the temperature rise of boom i, Ai its area and (xi, yi) its position from the centroid; A is the total boom area.
*/
