/* book exam traps: Using σ = E α ΔT on a free beam with a linear gradient. A free beam bows stress-free. | Forgetting the factor 1/2: a spar held straight carries ±E α ΔT/2 at its faces, not E α ΔT. | Calling the held-straight stress self-equilibrating. Its net force is zero but its net moment is not; the supports supply it. | Putting h in mm when the curvature is wanted per metre. | Leaving out the −E α Ti term in a boom section; the formula then gives the thermal "moment stress" only. */
